    {
      "name": "nextjs",
      "type": "claude-md",
      "version": "1.0.0",
      "description": "Next.js App Router specific conventions",
      "author": "xeldar",
      "tags": [
        "nextjs",
        "react",
        "app-router",
        "conventions"
      ],
      "files": [
        {
          "path": "template.md",
          "target": ".claude/templates/nextjs.md"
        }
      ],
      "dependencies": [],
      "conflicts": [],
      "claudeMd": "## Next.js App Router Conventions\n\n- Use Server Components by default, add 'use client' only when needed\n- Colocate loading.tsx, error.tsx, not-found.tsx with page.tsx\n- Use Route Handlers (route.ts) for API endpoints\n- Fetch data in Server Components, not in client-side effects\n- Use Next.js Image component for all images\n- Use next/link for all internal navigation\n- Use Server Actions for form mutations\n- Keep client components small and leaf-level"
    },
    {
      "name": "python",
      "type": "claude-md",
      "version": "1.0.0",
      "description": "Python project conventions",
      "author": "xeldar",
      "tags": [
        "python",
        "conventions",
        "guidelines"
      ],
      "files": [
        {
          "path": "template.md",
          "target": ".claude/templates/python.md"
        }
      ],
      "dependencies": [],
      "conflicts": [],
      "claudeMd": "## Python Conventions\n\n- Use type hints everywhere (Python 3.10+ syntax)\n- Format with ruff (or black + isort)\n- Use dataclasses or Pydantic for data structures\n- Prefer pathlib.Path over os.path\n- Use f-strings for string formatting\n- Follow PEP 8 naming: snake_case functions, PascalCase classes\n- Use `from __future__ import annotations` for forward references\n- Prefer list/dict comprehensions over map/filter"
    },
    {
      "name": "rust",
      "type": "claude-md",
      "version": "1.0.0",
      "description": "Rust project conventions",
      "author": "xeldar",
      "tags": [
        "rust",
        "conventions",
        "guidelines"
      ],
      "files": [
        {
          "path": "template.md",
          "target": ".claude/templates/rust.md"
        }
      ],
      "dependencies": [],
      "conflicts": [],
      "claudeMd": "## Rust Conventions\n\n- Use `Result<T, E>` for fallible operations, `Option<T>` for optional values\n- Prefer `thiserror` for library errors, `anyhow` for application errors\n- Use `clippy` with pedantic lints\n- Prefer iterators over manual loops\n- Use `derive` macros generously (Debug, Clone, PartialEq)\n- Keep `unsafe` blocks minimal and well-documented\n- Use `cargo fmt` for formatting"
    },
    {
      "name": "typescript",
      "type": "claude-md",
      "version": "1.0.0",
      "description": "TypeScript project conventions",
      "author": "xeldar",
      "tags": [
        "typescript",
        "conventions",
        "guidelines"
      ],
      "files": [
        {
          "path": "template.md",
          "target": ".claude/templates/typescript.md"
        }
      ],
      "dependencies": [],
      "conflicts": [],
      "claudeMd": "## TypeScript Conventions\n\n- Use strict TypeScript (`strict: true` in tsconfig)\n- Prefer `interface` over `type` for object shapes\n- Use discriminated unions for state management\n- No `any` — use `unknown` and narrow with type guards\n- Use `satisfies` operator for type-safe object literals\n- Prefer `const` assertions for literal types\n- Use barrel exports (`index.ts`) for public APIs\n- Keep types close to the code that uses them\n- Use generic constraints to make reusable utilities type-safe"
    },
